  "overview": {
    "en": "Daniel Bernoulli was a Swiss mathematician and physicist best known for his work in fluid dynamics. His most important contribution, Bernoulli's principle, describes the relationship between fluid speed and pressure, forming a cornerstone of aerodynamics.",
